{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Root cause CONFIRMED — runtime proof, not a source read\n\n**The gate.** `autodeploy.sh` computes the mcp delta at two sites and NEITHER consults `SECRETS_PATHS`:\n\n- `infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh:168` — `SECRETS_PATHS='infra/scripts/fetch-secrets.sh infra/terraform/ssm.tf'`\n- `:710-711` (pre-fix numbering) — the review-bot gate ORs it in:\n  `changed_range \"$bot_deployed\" \"$TARGET\" \"$BOT_PATHS\" || changed_range \"$bot_deployed\" \"$TARGET\" \"$SECRETS_PATHS\"`\n- `:729` and `:733` (pre-fix) — the mcp gate does not, on either the backoff-active or the backoff-clear arm: `changed_range \"$mcp_deployed\" \"$TARGET\" \"$MCP_PATHS\"`.\n\n**Runtime experiment (discriminating).** Added a parametrized test to the existing real-bash integration harness (`tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_mcp_bluegreen.py::_real_git_box`, which stubs the box binaries onto PATH and runs the SHIPPED script against a real git repo). Repo baseline extended with `infra/terraform/ssm.tf`; the target commit touches ONLY the secrets path. Observed pre-fix, for both `infra/scripts/fetch-secrets.sh` and `infra/terraform/ssm.tf`:\n\n```\ncmds=['tag compose-review-bot:latest compose-review-bot:prev',\n      'compose-build-review-bot', 'compose-up-review-bot']\njournal: \"review-bot sources or secrets changed; sync + refresh .env + rebuild + restart\"\njournal: \"deploy complete: env now reflects <target>\"\n```\n\nNo `compose-build-mcp`. No `run --name rebar-mcp-…`. The tick reports **complete** and stamps the target sha, so the delta is consumed and never retried.\n\nThis discriminates against the rival \"the bot's own fetch-secrets refresh covers mcp\". That refresh at `:667` does rewrite `$DEPLOY_REPO/infra/compose/.env`, and mcp's `.env` and `mcp-static-tokens.json` are the same on-disk files — but **no new mcp container is started**, and both artifacts are read once at container init (`mcp_run_new` passes `--env-file \"$COMPOSE_DIR/.env\"` and bind-mounts `-v \"$COMPOSE_DIR/mcp-static-tokens.json:/run/secrets/mcp-static-tokens.json:ro\"`, `:370-408`). The running server keeps serving the OLD values. `infra/runbooks/mcp-client-pats.md:200` states the same requirement independently: a PAT change needs a RESTART so the init-time verifier re-reads.\n\n**Live relevance holds.** The bearer PATs are exactly this path: `fetch-secrets.sh:201-231` reads `/rebar/prod/mcp-client-pat-{copilot,codex,claude}` and materializes `mcp-static-tokens.json` beside `.env`.\n\n## Defect legitimacy: `defect` (unmet obligation)\n\n`SECRETS_PATHS` exists solely so an SSM-backed env change reaches a container that consumes it (`autodeploy.sh:162-167`; `f600-525c-fd6d-4a3d` / incident 2731). The mcp block's own comment at `:750-755` states the invariant it violates: \"Without this an SSM PAT rotation never reaches the container … the next unrelated `src/rebar` change starts a container against the STALE file\" — the 2026-08-25 crash-loop, `receptive-houndy-nilgai`. The mcp gate never met that obligation.\n\n## Attribution: `6964-40bb-46c9-48a7` (panicky-sylphish-foxterrier)\n\n- `SECRETS_PATHS` introduced by `820159375abd` (2026-07-20, `rebar-ticket: f600-525c-fd6d-4a3d`).\n- `MCP_PATHS` and both mcp gate sites introduced by `2a0a4b19f2ab` (2026-08-25, `rebar-ticket: 6964-40bb-46c9-48a7`, \"infra: add mcp blue-green autodeploy target\") — `git log -S'MCP_PATHS=' -- infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh`.\n\nThe obligation predates the consumer by five weeks, so this is the missed-consumer-update case: the new mcp component consumes fetch-secrets output but its delta gate was written against `MCP_PATHS` alone. Attribution goes to the ticket that ADDED the gate, not to `f600`, which created the obligation and could not have known about a component that did not yet exist. Recording the divergence per protocol: a whole-file blame majority on `autodeploy.sh` would name neither.\n\n## Fix\n\n`autodeploy.sh` gains one `mcp_delta()` helper beside `changed()` that ORs `MCP_PATHS || SECRETS_PATHS`; both gate sites call it. Mirrors the bot gate exactly. The canonical `MCP_PATHS` declaration in the `mcp:` compose comment is annotated to say so.\n\n## Out of scope, with its actual remedy\n\nA pure SSM **value** rotation advances no git ref, so no git-delta gate can see it — by construction, not by omission. That path stays operator-driven via `infra/runbooks/mcp-client-pats.md`. This fix does not and cannot replace it.\n"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787952779674868915,"uuid":"1110c179-d4ac-4523-8e0c-eba3978229dd"}